1
00:04:57,500 --> 00:05:03,500
Passion Brought Them Together... Only Success Could Tear Them Apart!

2
00:09:55,000 --> 00:10:01,000
Up Close & Personal is a drama, romance film directed by Jon Avnet.

3
00:14:52,500 --> 00:14:58,500
Tally Atwater has a dream: to be a prime-time network newscaster.

4
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:56,000
She pursues this dream with nothing but ambition,
raw talent and a homemade demo tape.

5
00:24:47,500 --> 00:24:53,500
Warren Justice is a brilliant, hard edged, veteran newsman.

6
00:29:45,000 --> 00:29:51,000
He sees Tally has talent and becomes her mentor.

7
00:34:42,500 --> 00:34:48,500
Tally’s career takes a meteoric rise and she and Warren fall in love.

8
00:39:40,000 --> 00:39:46,000
The romance that results is as intense and revealing as television news itself.

9
00:44:37,500 --> 00:44:43,500
Yet, each breaking story, every videotaped crisis that brings them
together, also threatens to drive them apart...

10
00:49:35,000 --> 00:49:41,000
Warren Justice, played by Robert Redford.

11
00:54:32,500 --> 00:54:38,500
Tally Atwater, played by Michelle Pfeiffer.

12
00:59:30,000 --> 00:59:36,000
Marcia McGrath, played by Stockard Channing.

13
01:04:27,500 --> 01:04:33,500
Bucky Terranova, played by Joe Mantegna.

14
01:09:25,000 --> 01:09:31,000
Joanna Kennelly, played by Kate Nelligan.

15
01:14:22,500 --> 01:14:28,500
Ned Jackson, played by Glenn Plummer.

16
01:19:20,000 --> 01:19:26,000
Up Close & Personal is a 1996 American romantic drama film directed by Jon Avnet
from a screenplay written by Joan Didion and John Gregory Dunne.

17
01:24:17,500 --> 01:24:23,500
It stars Robert Redford as a news director and Michelle Pfeiffer as his protégée, with
Stockard Channing, Joe Mantegna, and Kate Nelligan in supporting roles.

18
01:29:15,000 --> 01:29:21,000
The screenplay began as an adaptation of Golden Girl: The Story of Jessica Savitch, a 1988 book by
Alanna Nash that recounted the troubled life of American news anchor Jessica Savitch.

19
01:34:12,500 --> 01:34:18,500
The finished picture, however, was greatly altered by commercial decisions on the part
of the producers, and bore little resemblance to Savitch's biography.

20
01:39:10,000 --> 01:39:16,000
Dunne, having spent eight years working on the script with his wife Didion, later wrote a book
describing his difficult experience, titled Monster: Living Off the Big Screen.

21
01:44:07,500 --> 01:44:13,500
"Because You Loved Me", the film's theme song written by Diane Warren and performed by
Celine Dion, was nominated for Best Original Song at the 69th Academy Awards.

22
01:49:05,000 --> 01:49:11,000
The film explores themes of career, miami,
florida, affectation, reporter, candid.

23
01:54:02,500 --> 01:54:08,500
The tone is emotional and intense.
